<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maysa Wali</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Maysa Wali Jaxateh Manneh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maysa Wali is remembered as the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guelowar">Guelowar</a> king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-sine">Sine</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serer">Serer</a> kingdom in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a>, in the 14th century. Tradition says the Guelowar came from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaabu-empire">Kaabu</a>, and that he was chosen as king for his wisdom. He founded the line of rulers titled Maad a Sinig, which lasted until the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahecor-diouf">Mahecor Diouf</a> in 1969.</p></div>
